lines += ['', '## Two-day scope (working outline, not confirmed dates)','Day 1: owner confirms coherent project; select four room views + dining table/chair/sideboard; prepare form-first product cards, source/camera locks and source rights notes.','Day 2: one real-photo light edit first, side-by-side review, then consistent project pass. For product shots isolate/clean product first; studio environment only after product acceptance. Inspect final dimensions and all ratios. Max 3 rounds/stage.','', '## Next edit step / dresser-01 continuity','Do not reuse rejected P1f_v1_APPROVED.png. True prior approved truth is dresser-01_P1f_TRUE-APPROVED.webp; for this NEW project use its own real source photographs, never the dresser render. Continuous edit chat per product; start on real source. Lock camera yaw, silhouette, part counts, seams, proportions, materials and colours. Separate light/background from product. Product card must be owner-confirmed before round 1. geometry_compare.py plus photobank.py fidelity and side-by-side original QA before each next stage. No recipes for an unchosen direction generated here.','', '## Dependencies / intake','Project membership and user choice; final output dimensions/placement; direction/style references; right to use originals/visible people; product cards and tolerances before image render. No logo, copy or CTA currently requested; proposed clean imagery without overlay requires owner confirmation for production.','No generation, paid credits, downloads, account calls or final render approval performed. Read-only originals, local review thumbnails only.','', '## Skills','TSST-CREATIVE-SK-019: bank source intake, manifest/provenance, deterministic review files, export state.','TSST-CREATIVE-SK-014: immutable product truth, staged edit method, owner source confirmation and numeric QA next step.','Skills skipped: none from assigned list. SK-011 not selected; no social layout requested.','skill_friction: photo-bank README method/QA skill directory pointers are stale; canonical build_index IDs used. Automated group names and piece tags are not reliable evidence of project membership; visual review required.']
